Created the Plone Aurora add-on. It renders Aurora's `/login` with the same sign-in choices as the Volto add-on -- a button for each identity provider, the magic link and, when `IDENTITY_SHOW_PLONE_LOGIN` or `config.settings.identity.showPloneLogin` allows it, the password form -- inside Aurora's own login frame and theme. A site with a single provider sends the visitor straight to it unless `IDENTITY_REDIRECT_TO_SOLE_PROVIDER` says otherwise. A sign-in starts at `/login-identity/start/<provider>` and finishes at `/login-identity`, the same callback path the Volto add-on uses, storing the session in Aurora's own cookie; a magic link arriving there signs in the same way. The backend is called through a virtual-host URL naming Aurora's public address, so the provider sends the user back to Aurora, and the backend's flow cookie is passed through to the browser and back. A signed-in user manages their sign-in methods at `/identities`, reached from the header's tools: the providers linked to their account, linking another one, removing one, and verifying or preferring the addresses on their profile. A completed link returns there. A user whose profile is missing required fields is held, on every page with the site's header, at `/complete-profile`, which names the fields and links to the edit form, and sent on to where they were going once it is complete; one asked which of several verified addresses is theirs answers at `/confirm-email`. On a site running the authorization server, `/applications` lists the applications a user has authorized, and withdraws one after asking. Such a site's consent screen is `/oauth-consent`, and Aurora serves the authorization server's endpoints -- `@@oauth-authorize`, `@@oauth-token`, `@@oauth-jwks`, `@@oauth-userinfo` and the discovery document -- by passing them on to the backend, sending the user's session to the authorization endpoint, so no reverse-proxy rule is needed for them. Translations come from `identity-core`'s catalogues, regenerated with `pnpm i18n`. Requires Plone Aurora 1.0.0-alpha.16 or later. @sneridagh
